+ *    reader protects with policy_rwlock. We clone it *outside* of the lock,
+ *    then swap the whole struct in place while holding policy_rwlock for
+ *    writing. Every allocation happens before the lock is taken, so nothing
+ *    can sleep in atomic context, and the swap is atomic for all readers.
